# 13. BST SEARCH

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## PROBLEM

Search for:

```
X
```

in a Binary Search Tree.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## BST PROPERTY

For node:

```
X

LEFT < X < RIGHT
```

Therefore:

If target < current:

```
go LEFT
```

If target > current:

```
go RIGHT
```

If equal:

```
FOUND
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## CODE

```
bool search(Node* root, int target) {

    if(root == nullptr)
        return false;

    if(root->data == target)
        return true;

    if(target < root->data)
        return search(
            root->left,
            target
        );

    return search(
        root->right,
        target
    );
}
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## KEY IDEA

You do NOT search both sides.

BST gives direction.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## MASTER STORY

```
             CURRENT
                │
      ┌─────────┼─────────┐
      │         │         │
   target <   equal    target >
      │         │         │
      ▼         ▼         ▼
    LEFT      FOUND      RIGHT
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## RECOGNITION

```
BST + search

    ↓

compare
    ↓
choose ONE side
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## COMPLEXITY

Average:

```
O(log N)
```

Worst case:

```
