   +
unweighted
   +
grid
```

Think:

```
BFS
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## WHY BFS?

BFS explores:

```
distance 0
   ↓
distance 1
   ↓
distance 2
   ↓
...
```

Therefore the first time we reach destination:

```
shortest path
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## DIRECTIONS

```
UP
DOWN
LEFT
RIGHT
```

Represent:

```
dr = {-1,1,0,0}
dc = {0,0,-1,1}
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## CODE TEMPLATE

```
queue<pair<int,int>> q;

q.push({sr, sc});

dist[sr][sc] = 0;

while(!q.empty()) {

    auto [r,c] = q.front();
    q.pop();

    for(int d = 0; d < 4; d++) {

        int nr = r + dr[d];
        int nc = c + dc[d];

        if(valid(nr,nc) &&
           notVisited(nr,nc)) {

            dist[nr][nc] =
                dist[r][c] + 1;

            q.push({nr,nc});
        }
    }
}
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## MASTER RULE

```
SHORTEST PATH
   +
UNWEIGHTED

    ↓

   BFS
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## IMPORTANT

