# 20. 0/1 KNAPSACK — TAKE / SKIP

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## PROBLEM

You have:

```
weights
values
capacity W
```

Each item can be:

```
TAKE once
```

OR:

```
SKIP
```

Maximize total value.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## FIRST RECOGNITION

Words:

```
choose items
capacity
maximize value
each item once
```

Think:

```
0/1 KNAPSACK
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## STATE

```
dp[i][w]
```

means:

```
maximum value using
first i items
with capacity w
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## CHOICE

For item i:

```
SKIP
```

OR:

```
TAKE
```

If weight fits:

```
take =
    value[i]
    +
    dp[i-1][w-weight[i]]
```

skip:

```
dp[i-1][w]
```

Therefore:

```
dp[i][w] =
    max(
        skip,
        take
    )
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## CODE

```
vector<vector<int>> dp(
    n+1,
    vector<int>(W+1, 0)
);

for(int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {

    for(int w = 0; w <= W; w++) {

        dp[i][w] =
            dp[i-1][w];

        if(weight[i-1] <= w) {

            dp[i][w] =
                max(
                    dp[i][w],
                    value[i-1] +
                    dp[
                        i-1
                    ][
                        w-weight[i-1]
                    ]
                );
        }
    }
}

cout << dp[n][W];
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## MASTER QUESTION

If every item can be:

```
TAKE
OR
SKIP
```

think:

```
DP
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## CRITICAL DIFFERENCE

0/1:

```
each item ONCE
```

Unbounded:

```
same item can be used repeatedly
```

This difference changes the transition / loop direction.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## RECOGNITION

```
capacity
value
weights
select subset
each item once

    ↓

0/1 KNAPSACK
```

